    "attribution": "NOT an allocator defect. Measured independently by the coordinator (diagnostics/pmo_offmanifold_reward_hacking_v1.json): gsk3b's fingerprint-RandomForest oracle REWARDS off-manifold chemistry, r(score,QED) = -0.433 and r(score,SA) = +0.684. An allocator that follows measured score correctly follows a corrupt signal. The new top parent is the 37-heavy-atom CC1C(C)C2CC3CC(=O)C2(C(C#N)C1NC1=C(P)C=C(Br)C(C(N)[IH]OOCNNCO)N1)C3(C)C.",
    "consequence": "Any gsk3b chemistry number from this controller measures the oracle, not the search. Read gsk3b on score only, or fix the oracle before reading its chemistry at all."
   }
